    <!--
        THIS COMMENT IS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT ON PURPOSE - a comment ABOVE <PermissionSet> breaks
        `sf` at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.
        The prose below lived in <description> until 2026-08-31, when a real deploy proved
        PermissionSet.description is capped at 255 characters (measured on usman-dpeg -
        "Description: data value too large: ... (max length=255)") - a DIFFERENT cap from
        CustomField.description (1000, also measured) and LWC .js-meta.xml <description> (255,
        also measured but a separate metadata type). This repo's established pattern for exceeding
        a description cap is to shorten <description> and move the full rationale here.

        NEW SET, not an edit to DPEG_Transaction_Edit or DPEG_Task_Edit, because a PermissionSet
        deploy replaces its entire fieldPermissions block and both of those are live hub files a
        concurrent session is changing. Assign alongside DPEG_Transaction_Edit.

        Wire access is scoped here to the Transaction team and admins only - no Accounting persona
        set exists and none was created.

        Checklist and Checklist Item are master-detail details, so viewAllRecords is left false
        deliberately: read on every Transaction already IS read on every checklist under
        ControlledByParent, and DPEG_Transaction_Edit grants viewAllRecords on Transaction.

        Also carries the FLS grant on Critical_Date__c.Transaction__c, which became a
        permissionable field the moment its required flag was relaxed and is invisible without it.
    -->
