    <!--
        ADDED 2026-08-31, POST-DEPLOY FIX. Checklist__c is Master-Detail to Transaction__c, and this
        set's own Read grant on Checklist__c was refused outright: "Permission Read Checklist__c
        depends on permission(s): Read Transaction__c" - measured to be a WITHIN-THE-SAME-FILE
        dependency, not an org-wide or co-assigned-set one: the identical error persisted even in a
        dry-run that included DPEG_Transaction_Edit/DPEG_Transaction_View (which already grant
        Transaction__c Read) in the SAME deploy transaction. This repo already has the correct
        precedent for this exact rule - DPEG_PropertyMgmt_Edit grants both Meter__c (master) and
        Utility_Bill__c (child) in one file for the same reason. This block is Read-only,
        deliberately minimal: it exists ONLY to satisfy the master-detail dependency, not to
        duplicate DPEG_Transaction_Edit's fuller Transaction__c grant (create/edit/viewAllRecords) -
        assign this set alongside DPEG_Transaction_Edit exactly as originally intended; a user
        holding both simply gets the union.
    -->
    <objectPermissions>
